    "https://brynmawr.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Bryn-Mawr-College-Campus/Full-Cook_JR-000321": {
      "title": "Full Cook",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Full Cook Bryn Mawr College: Erdman Dining Location: Bryn Mawr College Campus Job Description: Bryn Mawr College is seeking   Full   Cook to perform a variety of   related to the preparation and presentation of all meals and catering at Wyndham and other Dining locations.       About the Institution:   Since its founding in 1885, Bryn Mawr College has been the preeminent college for women interested in the pursuit of wisdom necessary to challenge the world's expectations. With its pioneering American Collegiate Gothic architecture and picturesque landscape, our campus is recognized as one of the most beautiful in the country. Located less than 15 miles from Philadelphia, and within 2-3 hours of New York City, Baltimore, and Washington, DC, Bryn Mawr’s location offers easy access to public transportation and endless recreation, dining,   retail,   and cultural activities.     Schedule & Benefits:   Bryn Mawr is committed to building and sustaining a campus community where faculty and staff can thrive.   The College offers competitive salaries and   excellent benefits .   This full-time staff position   has a schedule of   40 hours   per   week; the   current   schedule   for this position   is   10:30 am   to 7pm,   Friday   through   Tuesday   during normal weeks of the semester   but varies   during breaks, summer & around holidays.   The successful candidate will be   eligible for   22 days   of vacation per year, three days personal leave, generous holiday time (including an extended   paid   winter break between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day), sick leave, short- and long-term disability, life insurance, medical, dental, and vision, retirement, paid parental leave, tuition opportunities, and more. Waiting periods may apply.     Core Responsibilities   Food Preparation &   Quality   High-Quality Cooking: Prepare entrees, soups, side dishes, and catering orders for students, staff, and college guests. Cook in small batches whenever possible to ensure maximum freshness ,   prevent overproduction   and quality.     Recipe & Yield Management: Prepare food according to production sheets. Assess food quality and, after consulting with a manager, adjust recipes as needed for proper yield and standards. Make approved substitutions based on meal counts.   Service Line Operations: Set up, decorate, and   maintain   the service line. Ensure all wells are filled, items are properly labeled, and   appropriate utensils   are available. Replenish food throughout service and instruct servers on correct   portion   sizes.   Food Waste   Tracking & Management: Actively   utilize   the   Leanpath   automated food waste tracking system to log all kitchen trimmings, expired items, and overproduction.   Food Safety, Sanitation, & Compliance   Temperature Control: Strictly   maintain , monitor, and log proper food temperatures). Take immediate corrective action and report issues to supervisors if standards are breached.   Regulatory Compliance: Adhere to all health and sanitation standards outlined by   ServSafe , local health authorities (Montgomery County), and Bryn Mawr College Dining Services.   Kitchen Cleanliness: Clean and   maintain   food preparation equipment. Coordinate with kitchen staff and student workers to manage the kitchen’s overall cleaning schedule.   Cross-Contact   & Cross-Contamination   Prevention:   Maintain   strict separation of ingredients during prep, cooking, and service to prevent allergen cross-contact.   C ommunicate any ingredient changes or recipe substitutions to management to ensure labeling accuracy and student safety.   Leftover Management:   Properly store   leftover food   in accordance with   ServSafe   guidelines and   consult with the manager to   determine   how leftovers will be   safely   utilized .   Allergen Identification & Labeling:   Work with   culinary   team   to ensure   all foo d served   is promptly and correctly labeled with department standards .   Leadership   &   Communication   Work independently under limited management direction. Prioritize and organize daily workloads as directed ;   instruct   and   guide general kitchen staff and student workers.   Interact professionally with students, catering clients, college staff, and guests. Actively   assist   managers and collaborate with the receiver to ensure inventory is pulled for the next day's meals.   Accurately complete and   submit   daily production sheets and temperature charts to management.   Job Requirements & Working Conditions   Equipment Proficiency: Must safely and effectively operate a variety of commercial kitchen equipment, including but not limited to: knives, slicers, deep fryers, tilt skillets, grills, various ovens, mixers with attachments, kettles, warmer boxes, steam lines, thermometers, steamers, ranges, and buffalo choppers.   Scheduling Flexibility: Requires a highly flexible schedule to support campus events, Board Plan functions, and catering services. Hours and schedules will change with limited notice based on catering volume and activity (catering   operates   365 days   a year).   Essential Personnel: Because Bryn Mawr is a residential college, Dining Services staff are classified as essential personnel and   are required to   work during campus closures or emergencies as needed.   Other Duties: Perform   additional   job-related   tasks as   assigned by management.     Qualifications:   Ability to read and follow written instructions .   Basic arithmetic skills   required   for baking, measuring , other   kitchen responsibilities .     Ability to   stand, sit, stoop, bend down, kneel, climb stairs, at times for extended periods,   lift   to   50   lbs.   and   heavier items   (with or without   assistance ).   Frequent physical effort involves   lifting   heavy weights, stopping   standing   and bending for extended periods of time .    This is a hands- on working   supervisor.   Good oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills.    Ability to move between   workstations   and within campus buildings.   Ability to wo rk in variable and at times, adverse conditions ( e.g.   hot and   cold weather , indoors and outdoors).   This position is considered essential staff and may be   required   to work during inclement weather   (weather differential pay available for instances where   College administration applies a weather emergency designation, based on inclement weather conditions).   Demonstrate the ability to lead and supervise other workers.   ServSafe   Certification: Annual in-house training and recertification are provided by   Dining Services   and must be successfully completed   to   maintain   certification .   Food Allergen Certification :   Requirement to pass   AllerTrain   or   FareCheck   certification. Annual in-house training and recertification are provided by the College and must be successfully completed yearly.   Successful completion of satisfactory references, background checks, and pre-employment physical.   To apply, upload your complete application package as a single PDF document. A complete application package includes: 1) cover letter and 2) resume. Application review will continue until the position is filled. To initiate your application, use the APPLY button. Weekly Hours: 40"
    },
    "https://brynmawr.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Bryn-Mawr-College-Campus/Director-of-Alumnae-i-Relations---Development-Marketing---Communications_JR-000386": {
      "title": "Director of Alumnae/i Relations & Development Marketing & Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Director of Alumnae/i Relations & Development Marketing & Communications Bryn Mawr College: Alumnae Relations & Development Location: Bryn Mawr College Campus Job Description: About the Institution: Since its founding in 1885, Bryn Mawr College has been the preeminent college for women interested in the pursuit of wisdom necessary to challenge the world's expectations. With its pioneering American Collegiate Gothic architecture and picturesque landscape, our campus is recognized as one of the most beautiful in the country. Located less than 15 miles from Philadelphia, and within 2-3 hours of New York City, Baltimore, and Washington, DC, Bryn Mawr’s location offers easy access to public transportation and endless recreation, dining, retail, and cultural activities. Position Overview: Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Constituent Engagement, the Director of Alumnae/i Relations & Development Marketing & Communications plays a key part in advancing the communication goals of the Alumnae/i Relations and Development (ARD) department to engage alumnae/i, families, faculty, staff, and friends. The Director will manage and oversee the work of two direct reports: The Assistant Director of Marketing and Communications and the Senior Communications Specialist and will oversee, conceive and carry out marketing strategies and communications in collaboration with colleagues in the departments of Alumnae/i Relations and Development and the Office of Communications and Marketing. Position Responsibilities: Work closely with the Constituent Engagement team to create a comprehensive strategy for short- and long-term donor growth of The Bryn Mawr Fund including the two Graduate Funds. Work with the AVP for Constituent Engagement to develop and execute a strategic communications plan each year to maximize fundraising results through segmented cross-channeled mass communications involving direct mail; phone-a-thon; email; website, texting, and social media. Ensure Advancement communications align with institutional messaging, brand standards, and the College's mission and values. Partner closely and collaborate with the Office of Communications and Marketing and other campus partners to ensure coordinated, strategic, and effective messaging. Manage and oversee the work of two direct reports. Manage and oversee creation and production, from draft through distribution of final product, communications to Bryn Mawr’s constituencies. Types of projects include targeted short-term online giving campaigns, brochures, letters, emails, inserts, invitations, web site content, and ads. Ensure error-free content and successful completion of marketing projects by managing production schedules, data pulls, and tracking costs and expenditures for each project. Show measurable results, which include bringing direct mail, phone-a-thon, texting, and online appeal results to a \"higher\" level in terms of increased giving, donor participation growth, or demonstrating procedural improvements. Research trends in solicitation marketing. May perform other duties as assigned. Schedule & Benefits: Bryn Mawr is committed to building and sustaining a campus community where faculty and staff can thrive. This full-time staff position has a standard schedule of 35 hours per week and is eligible for hybrid remote work.  The College offers competitive salaries and excellent benefits , including 22 days of vacation per year, three days personal leave, generous holiday time (including an extended winter break between Christmas Eve & New Year’s Day), sick leave, disability plans, life insurance, medical, dental, and vision, retirement, paid parental leave, tuition opportunities, and more. Waiting periods may apply. While no one person may possess all the qualifications listed below, the ideal candidate will have many of the following professional experiences and characteristics. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree is required. A minimum of five years of progressively responsible and relevant experience in fundraising, with particular experience in higher education annual giving, communications, and marketing. Management experience is required. Strong computer skills, for composing correspondence, list management, and data analysis. Knowledge of internet technology and trends in giving. Excellent written and oral communication skills and demonstrated ability to proofread are key. Ability to exercise and maintain discretion, sound judgment, and confidentiality. Must possess a high level of motivation and organization with exceptional attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple projects and prioritize tasks effectively. Maintenance of deadlines and achievement of ambitious goals are a priority. Must demonstrate the ability to work outside of normal business hours. Able to work well in a complex and/or team-oriented environment. Must have an appreciation for the value of a liberal arts education in a culturally diverse community. Key Relationships:  This position reports to the Associate Vice President for Constituent Engagement and may also have direct contact with various members of the Alumnae/i Relations and Development team, College community, including the President’s Office, Board of Trustees, the Office of Communications and Marketing, the Graduate Schools, faculty, administrators, alumnae/i, families, and students. To apply, upload your complete application package as a single PDF document. A complete application package includes: 1) cover letter and 2) resume. Application review will continue until the position is filled. To initiate your application, use the APPLY button. Weekly Hours: 35"
    },
    "https://brynmawr.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Bryn-Mawr-College-Campus/Project-Manager--Workday-Student_JR-000380": {
      "title": "Project Manager, Workday Student",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Project Manager, Workday Student Bryn Mawr College: Office of CIO and Director of Libraries Location: Bryn Mawr College Campus Job Description: Position Overview: The Department of Library & Information Technology Services seeks a full-time Project Manager for a project-funded, full-time, term-limited position with an estimated duration of three years. This is an at will position, contingent upon available funding and continued employment in good standing. The Project Manager plays a key leadership role in planning and delivering the Workday Student implementation at Bryn Mawr College. Reporting to the Associate Vice President, Library & Information Technology Services and working closely with functional leads, technical teams, senior stakeholders, and campus partners, the Project Manager coordinates work across functional, technical, institutional, and vendor teams to ensure clear plans, effective governance, timely decision-making, and successful execution. The role supports disciplined project delivery while fostering collaboration, accountability, and organizational readiness throughout a complex enterprise transformation. About the Institution: Since its founding in 1885, Bryn Mawr College has been the preeminent college for women interested in the pursuit of wisdom necessary to challenge the world's expectations. With its pioneering American Collegiate Gothic architecture and picturesque landscape, our campus is recognized as one of the most beautiful in the country. Located less than 15 miles from Philadelphia, and within 2-3 hours of New York City, Baltimore, and Washington, DC, Bryn Mawr’s location offers easy access to public transportation and endless recreation, dining, retail, and cultural activities. Schedule & Benefits: Bryn Mawr is committed to building and sustaining a campus community where faculty and staff can thrive. The College offers competitive salaries and excellent benefits. This full-time, term-limited staff position has an anticipated schedule of 35 hours per week and is eligible for vacation, personal leave, generous holiday time, sick leave, short- and long-term disability, life insurance, medical, dental, and vision, retirement, paid parental leave, tuition opportunities, and more. Waiting periods may apply. Characteristic Responsibilities: Project Leadership & Delivery Lead end-to-end planning and execution of the Workday Student implementation. Own the project framework, methodology, and delivery approach. Establish and maintain integrated project plans, timelines, milestones, and deliverables. Identify, manage, and mitigate risks, issues, and dependencies across project phases.   Operational and Organizational Leadership Coordinate work across functional and technical teams, ensuring alignment with institutional priorities. Facilitate structured decision-making and issue resolution across diverse stakeholder groups. Ensure clarity of roles, responsibilities, and expectations across project participants. Support continuity of project execution during periods of organizational or leadership transition.   Program, Portfolio, and Governance Management Contribute to PMO governance processes, including steering committee preparation and status reporting. Align project execution with PMO standards, prioritization frameworks, and portfolio objectives. Manage cross-project dependencies within the Workday platform and broader PMO portfolio. Provide clear, consistent reporting on progress, risks, and decisions to leadership. Use practical AI-enabled tools and workflows to reduce administrative burden, improve meeting follow-through, and support timely coordination across project workstreams.   Stakeholder, Vendor, and Partnership Management Serve as the primary interface between internal project teams and external implementation partners. Coordinate with functional leads representing key institutional areas (e.g., Registrar, Finance, Academic Affairs). Build strong relationships with stakeholders to support alignment, engagement, and accountability. Ensure effective collaboration across institutional and vendor teams.   Change Management Partnership Partner closely with Change Management leadership to align delivery plans with communication, training, and adoption strategies. Support a coordinated approach to stakeholder readiness and institutional transition. Reinforce alignment between project milestones and organizational change activities. Participate in change management activities. Other duties as assigned.   Qualifications: Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Experience in higher education or similarly complex, mission-driven organizations. Demonstrated experience with Workday Platform or comparable ERP systems. Significant experience leading large-scale enterprise system implementations. Demonstrated ability to manage complex, cross-functional projects with multiple stakeholders and dependencies. Experience working with external implementation partners and consultants. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate complex project information for diverse audiences. Comfort using AI-enabled productivity tools to support project coordination, documentation, and communication in a responsible and practical way. Successful completion of satisfactory background checks.   Preferred Qualifications Experience with Workday Student or comparable student information systems. PMP certification or coursework.   Leadership Attributes The successful candidate will be: A disciplined project leader who combines structured execution with adaptability. A clear communicator who builds trust across technical and functional stakeholders. Skilled at navigating complexity, ambiguity, and competing priorities. Collaborative and solutions-oriented, with a focus on delivering outcomes. To apply, upload your complete application package as a single PDF document. A complete application package includes: 1) cover letter, 2) resume, and 3) contact information for three professional references. Application review will continue until the position is filled. To initiate your application, use the APPLY button. Weekly Hours: 35"
    },
    "https://brynmawr.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Bryn-Mawr-College-Campus/Benefits---Wellness-Specialist_JR-000379": {
      "title": "Benefits & Wellness Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Benefits & Wellness Specialist Bryn Mawr College: Human Resources Location: Bryn Mawr College Campus Job Description: Position Overview: The Office of Human Resources at Bryn Mawr College invites applications for a Benefits & Wellness Specialist to join our collaborative team. At Bryn Mawr, people, purpose, and learning intersect—and our HR team plays a critical role in cultivating a workplace where faculty and staff can thrive.   In this role, you will help ensure that Bryn Mawr College's comprehensive benefits programs are delivered with care, accuracy, and exceptional service. Working closely with the Director of Employment & Benefits, you will support employee benefit, leave, and wellness programs, Open Enrollment, communications, and partnerships and serve as a trusted resource for employees navigating benefits and leaves (e.g., FMLA, parental, leave, and short-term disability). About the Institution:  Since its founding in 1885, Bryn Mawr College has been the preeminent college for women interested in the pursuit of wisdom necessary to challenge the world's expectations. With its pioneering American Collegiate Gothic architecture and picturesque landscape, our campus is recognized as one of the most beautiful in the country. Located less than 15 miles from Philadelphia, and within 2-3 hours of New York City, Baltimore, and Washington, DC, Bryn Mawr’s location offers easy access to public transportation and endless recreation, dining, retail, and cultural activities.  Schedule & Benefits:  Bryn Mawr is committed to building and sustaining a campus community where faculty and staff can thrive. This full-time position has a standard schedule of 35 hours per week and is eligible for hybrid remote work up to one day per week.  The College offers competitive salaries and  excellent benefits , including 22 days of vacation per year, three days personal leave, generous holiday time (including an extended winter break between Christmas Eve & New Year’s Day), 10% employer retirement contribution, sick leave, disability plans, life insurance, medical, dental, and vision, paid parental leave, tuition opportunities, and more. Waiting periods may apply.  Characteristic Responsibilities   Benefits Administration & Employee Support  Serve as a primary resource for employees regarding health, retirement, leave, and ancillary benefit programs, delivering exceptional customer service.   Administer a comprehensive portfolio of benefit programs and opportunities, including medical, dental, vision, retirement, disability, paid time off, tuition, COBRA, EAP, childcare, retiree, and other benefit offerings.   Partner with the Director of Employment & Benefits to plan, coordinate, and administer the annual Open Enrollment process, including employee communications, educational materials, enrollment tracking, and collaboration with HRIS and external vendors to ensure accurate enrollment and census data.  Audit benefit data, maintain accurate enrollment records, and manage benefit-related responsibilities, including the Benefits email inbox.   Maintain and update benefit information on the Human Resources website.   Collaborate with the Director of Employment & Benefits and campus partners to support employee wellness initiatives throughout the year.    Employee Health & Wellness Develop, coordinate, and promote comprehensive programs, ensuring access to resources that promote health, wellbeing, and overall workplace experience. Serve as a resource and advocate, helping employees understand and access available health and wellbeing resources. Plan and execute wellness initiatives, campaigns, communications, workshops, and educational events throughout the year. Partner with benefits providers, vendors, and internal stakeholders to deliver engaging wellness programs and resources. Coordinate health screenings in collaboration with the Health Center, wellness assessments, fitness initiatives, and other preventive health programs. Manage wellness calendars, communications, program coordination, and related administrative activities.   Benefits Operations  Manage relationships with benefit vendors and serve as the primary point of contact for benefit billing and plan administration.   Download, reconcile, and review vendor invoices; process payments through Workday using purchase orders and service invoice requests.   Monitor monthly carrier invoices, reconcile billing discrepancies, and ensure timely and accurate payment of benefit expenses.   Coordinate with HRIS and external vendors to maintain accurate census and enrollment files.     Leave Administration  Administer leave programs, including Family and Medical Leave (FMLA), Parental Leave, Workers' Compensation, and Short- and Long-Term Disability.   Serve as the primary point of contact for employees requesting or utilizing leave, providing guidance on eligibility, required documentation, and available benefits.   Maintain regular communication with employees and managers throughout the leave process and ensure receipt of appropriate status updates and return to work clearances. Facilitate leave-related documentation, wage verifications, insurance information, and other required communications.   Manage employee benefit contributions during paid and unpaid leave, including coordinating direct payments, as appropriate.    May perform other duties as assigned.    Qualifications   Bachelor's degree in human resources or related field required. Minimum four years of full-time, progressive experience in Human Resources/Benefits. CEBS, SHRM-CP, and/or PHR certifications a plus. Knowledge of HR best practices and employment laws.  Ability to work collaboratively with HR team members, faculty, staff, and students.  Strong interpersonal, communication, and conflict-resolution skills.  Ability to exercise and maintain discretion, sound judgment, and confidentiality.  Successful completion of satisfactory background checks.  Higher Ed and Workday experience preferred.  To apply, upload your complete application package as a single PDF document. A complete application package includes: 1) cover letter, 2) resume, and 3) contact information for three professional references. Application review will continue until the position is filled. To initiate your application, use the APPLY button. Weekly Hours: 35"
    },
    "https://brynmawr.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Bryn-Mawr-College-Campus/Public-History-Research-Fellow_JR-000351": {
      "title": "Research  Fellow, Public Humanities",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Research Fellow, Public Humanities Bryn Mawr College: LITS_TEMP Location: Bryn Mawr College Campus Job Description: Bryn Mawr College invites applications for a   public historian, archivist,   scholar ,   or journalist with   expertise   in post-nineteenth - century American collegiate life, women’s/gender history,   African American   history and/or intersectional histories, and digital scholarship .    Reporting directly to the Vice President, Chief Information   Officer,   and Constance A. Jones Director of Libraries, the successful candidate will   partner with   the   Bryn Mawr College community on a series of initiatives related to   Bryn Mawr College Histories   and its place in the present higher education landscape.      About the Institution:   Since its founding in 1885, Bryn Mawr College has been the preeminent college for women interested in the pursuit of wisdom necessary to challenge the world's expectations. With its pioneering American Collegiate Gothic architecture and picturesque landscape, our campus is recognized as one of the most beautiful in the country. Located less than 15 miles from Philadelphia and within 2-3 hours of New York City, Baltimore, and Washington, DC, Bryn Mawr offers easy access to public transportation and endless recreation, dining, retail, and cultural activities.     Schedule & Benefits:   Bryn Mawr is committed to building and sustaining a campus community where faculty and staff can thrive.   The College offers competitive salaries and   excellent benefits . This   is a   full-time , temporary   staff position   for a   12-month   term ,   commencing   on or about   September   1 5 , 2026 ,   and concluding   on or about   September   15 , 2027 .    The position   has an anticipated schedule of 35 hours per week and is eligible for   22 days   of vacation per year, three days   of   personal leave, generous holiday time (including an extended winter break between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day), sick leave, life insurance, medical, dental, and vision, retirement, and more. Waiting periods may apply.     Characteristic Responsibilities:   Drawing on work completed at the College over the last few years through   Who Built Bryn Mawr ,   Art Remediating Campus Histories (ARCH) , and related initiatives, this researcher will:    Build a comprehensive historical timeline of the College and future research agenda, framing existing   scholarships   and   identifying   areas and periods where   additional   scholarly examination is   warranted .   Identify   primary historical themes and threads through archival research and literature review to best illustrate the story of Bryn Mawr College and its graduates' impact on   the world.   Partner with College leadership and constituents to review and integrate historical storytelling   and   institutional   impact   into public-facing venues.   Conduct targeted historical research as needed to inform College communications   and marketing , including presidential writing and speaking, materials for members of the on-campus community, alumn ae/ i   publications, recruitment   materials,   etc.    Collaborate with leadership in the faculty, student, staff, and   alumnae / a   communities to connect the College’s history to its future .       Qualifications:    Master's degree in history, public history, museum studies, or a related field with equivalent education, training, and/or experience.   (PhD or terminal degree preferred).   Demonstrated experience in archival or public   history   research and teaching.   Strong record of community-engaged scholarship or programming.   Demonstrated interpersonal and communication skills as   they   relate to   the   community.   Experience   in creative, innovative, and engaging storytelling .   Experience and comfort with digital scholarship techniques and tools   is   preferred.    We further seek someone familiar with the liberal arts and prepared and eager to collaborate with all members of our community in conducting this research.    Successful completion of satisfactory background checks.   To apply, upload your complete application package as a single PDF document. A complete application package includes: 1) cover letter; 2) resume; and 3) names/contact information for three professional references. Application review will continue until the position is filled. To initiate your application, use the APPLY button. Weekly Hours: 35"
    },
    "https://brynmawr.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Bryn-Mawr-College-Campus/Head-Strength-and-Conditioning-Coach-and-Fitness-Center-Director_JR-000363": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Strength & Conditioning; Director, Fitness Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Head Strength and Conditioning Coach and Fitness Center Director Bryn Mawr College: Athletics & Physical Education Location: Bryn Mawr College Campus Job Description: The position supports 12 Varsity athletics teams in strength and conditioning. Demonstrates knowledge of and   proficiency   in anatomy and physiology, exercise science, fundamental and Olympic-style weight-lifting exercises, and sport-specific speed,   agility   and quickness training. The position should also   possess   a passion for women’s athletics. Able to instruct, to communicate technique refinement through various teaching methods, and to demand a higher level of performance through positive feedback and cues .   About the Institution:   Since its founding in 1885, Bryn Mawr College has been the preeminent college for women interested in the pursuit of wisdom necessary to challenge the world's expectations. With its pioneering American Collegiate Gothic architecture and picturesque landscape, our campus is recognized as one of the most beautiful in the country. Located less than 15 miles from Philadelphia, and within 2-3 hours of New York City, Baltimore, and Washington, DC, Bryn Mawr’s location offers easy access to public transportation and endless recreation, dining, retail, and cultural activities.   Schedule & Benefits:   Bryn Mawr is committed to building and sustaining a campus community where faculty and staff can thrive. The College offers competitive salaries and   excellent benefits , including but not limited to a 10% retirement contribution. This full-time,   exempt   position has   an anticipated   schedule of 35 hours per week, year-round ( 1,820 hours   annualized).   Position Responsibilities:   The head strength and conditioning coach plans and executes strength and conditioning programming of our Varsity athletics teams. The position is   required   to teach exercise form and technique on all main strength and power lifts and on all accessory work, to coach athletes to spot and   assist   with relevant form cues, and to teach running and SAQ form. The position is also responsible for the overall safety of the weight room facility.    The position is expected to do the following:   Manage strength and conditioning programming through the program   Teambuildr   for competitive and off-season segments of an athletic season.   Work collaboratively with athletic training to develop programming that challenges   student athletes   while mitigating injuries.   Meet regularly with head coaches and athletic trainers.   Develop strength and conditioning strategic plan including long- and short-term goals for athletes and Varsity athletic teams.   Provide direct   reports   for the Assistant Strength and Conditioning Coach.   Fitness Center Director:   Oversees and directs the operations,   maintenance   and upkeep of the fitness center.   Recruit,   train,   and supervise the student workers for the fitness center.   Work with Associate AD and Conferences and Events to manage summer programming .    Has day-to-day direction and oversight of entire facility during summer months .     Develop and coordinate Fit Club programming. Hire fit club instructors. Manage and schedule fit club classes.    Provide orientations for faculty, staff, students to fitness   center .   Oversee facility membership. Expected to have over $7,000 in membership revenue.   Maintain facility calendar and webpage.   Develop and   maintain   policies of the fitness center.   Provides budget management and oversight for the fitness center   operating   annual budget.   Coordinate reunion activities and oversight with Alumnae/ i   Relations and Development .      Qualifications:    Bachelor's   degree is   required . Master’s degree preferred.   Certification in Strength and Conditioning or Personal Training is   required .    The NCSA or USA weightlifting certifications are preferred.    Knowledge of Olympic lifts is   required .    Additional   instructor certifications (Yoga, Spinning, Kettlebells, TRX, etc.) are welcome.    Additional   classes or duties may be assigned based upon experience and skill set.    Adult CPR/AED certification is   required .   Successful   completion   of satisfactory background checks.    Some lifting, carrying equipment, and walking   are required .       Ability to stand for   long periods   of time .    Ability to work outside of a variety of weather conditions.     To apply, upload your complete application package as a single PDF document. A complete application package includes: 1) cover letter; 2) resume; and 3) names/contact information for three professional references. Application review will continue until the position is filled. To   initiate   your application, use the APPLY button. Weekly Hours: 35"
    },
